findings:
- finding_id: C1
  title: from_file_or_default swallows ALL errors including parse and permission failures
  weight: 8
  phase_ideal: dev
  caught: false
  caught_by: null
  evidence: TEA mentions 'no silent error swallowing on connection failures' but no
    test specifically targets from_file_or_default swallowing parse/permission errors.
    Reviewer did not flag this. Dev likely implemented unwrap_or_default pattern unchecked.
- finding_id: I1
  title: CliError Display leaks internal details to stderr (CWE-209)
  weight: 5
  phase_ideal: reviewer
  caught: true
  caught_by: reviewer
  evidence: "Reviewer flagged '[HIGH] ServerError Display leaks raw server response\
    \ body \u2014 CWE-209' noting that error variants pass raw HTTP response body\
    \ to the operator and the test is vacuous. Also noted eprintln!('error: {e}')\
    \ in main.rs. TEA wrote a CWE-209 test but reviewer found it was vacuously true."
- finding_id: I2
  title: "SiemClient.tenant_id uses raw String \u2014 header injection risk (CWE-113)"
  weight: 5
  phase_ideal: tea
  caught: true
  caught_by: reviewer
  evidence: Reviewer flagged '[MEDIUM] tenant field is raw String, not TenantId newtype
    at cli.rs:22, client.rs:7' noting axiathon-core exports TenantId and it should
    be used. Also flagged '[HIGH] set_token/set_tenant bypass header injection validation'
    (CWE-113). TEA also wrote header injection tests but the underlying type issue
    was caught by reviewer.
- finding_id: I3
  title: Dependencies use direct version strings instead of workspace = true
  weight: 3
  phase_ideal: dev
  caught: false
  caught_by: null
  evidence: Reviewer marked '[VERIFIED] All workspace dependencies correctly declared
    in root Cargo.toml' but did not check whether crate-level Cargo.toml uses workspace
    = true vs direct version strings. The 6 deps using direct versions were not flagged.
- finding_id: I4
  title: "Config token field silently ignored \u2014 secret left on disk"
  weight: 5
  phase_ideal: reviewer
  caught: true
  caught_by: reviewer
  evidence: 'Reviewer flagged ''[MEDIUM] RawConfig silently ignores unknown fields
    at config.rs:5-9'' noting no #[serde(deny_unknown_fields)] and that a token =
    ''...'' field is silently ignored with no warning.'
- finding_id: I5
  title: "Vacuously true test \u2014 assertion is None || true"
  weight: 5
  phase_ideal: tea
  caught: false
  caught_by: null
  evidence: No phase identified the vacuously true assert!(config.server().is_none()
    || ...) pattern. The reviewer found a different vacuous test (ServerError display)
    but not this specific one in config_loading tests.
- finding_id: I6
  title: "Test with zero assertions \u2014 only checks non-panic"
  weight: 5
  phase_ideal: tea
  caught: false
  caught_by: null
  evidence: No phase flagged the test with zero assertions that only checks non-panic
    via 'let _ = config;'. TEA wrote config tests but did not ensure all tests had
    meaningful assertions on default config values.
